/-!
# Regular ideal sheaves are of finite type and quasi-coherent

A regular, Koszul-regular, `H₁`-regular or quasi-regular sheaf of ideals on a scheme is locally
generated by finitely many sections, hence of finite type, and a sheaf of ideals on a scheme
which is locally generated by sections is quasi-coherent.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isFiniteType_of_isRegularIdealSheaf` and
  `…isQuasicoherent_of_isRegularIdealSheaf`: **Stacks tag 063F** for regular ideal sheaves.
* `…isFiniteType_of_isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf` and `…isQuasicoherent_of_isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf`:
  the Koszul-regular case.
* `…isFiniteType_of_isH1RegularIdealSheaf` and `…isQuasicoherent_of_isH1RegularIdealSheaf`: the
  `H₁`-regular case.
* `…isFiniteType_of_isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf` and `…isQuasicoherent_of_isQuasiRegularIdealSheaf`:
  the quasi-regular case.

## Implementation notes

All four regularity conditions of Stacks tag 063D have the same shape: near every point of the
support of `O_X/J` the ideal sheaf is generated by a *finite* family of sections, the four
conditions differing only in what is required of that family.  Only the generation is used here,
so the four cases are instances of one statement,
`isFiniteType_of_locallyGenerated_on_quotient_support`, whose only extra work is the complement
of the support: away from it the unit section already lies in `J`, so `J` is generated there by
the one-element family `1`.

Turning a finite generating family over an open set into Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` for the restriction of `J` asks for the induced map from a
finite free module to be an epimorphism.  That is checked by local surjectivity of the underlying
map of presheaves of abelian groups, which is exactly the statement that a section of `J` is,
near every point, an `O_X`-combination of the generators — the content of
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.mem_generatedIdealOn_iff` read through
`exists_nhds_germ_eq`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Lemma 31.20.3 (Tag 063F)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063F)
* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.20.1 (Tag 063D)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 26.10.1 (Tag 01IN)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01IN)
-/

@[expose] public section

